[Page:Graphics]
PageContent=#INCLUDE(GraphicsContent)

[GraphicsContent]
<h2 class="ref-section" id="loading-screen">Loading screen</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The picture loaded into #R$4000(screen RAM) before the game starts.
</div>

#SCR2,tindex=1,alpha=0(loading_screen)

<h2 class="ref-section" id="title-logo">Title logo</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The KRAKOUT wordmark on the front-end title screen, a 14-column by 3-row block of
8×8 cells. The #R$BEF9(cell bitmaps) are stored in order, and the #R$C049(per-cell
attributes) that give the wordmark its color follow them. The render below
reads both:
</div>

#UDGTABLE { #UDGARRAY14,7,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($BEF9-$C041-8)[$C049-$C072](title_logo) } TABLE#

<h2 class="ref-section" id="character-font">Character font</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The game's own 8×8 character set, shown here from 0 to Z. The #R$8FB9(font entry) charts every glyph
against its character code.
</div>

#FONT36921,43,71,2,tindex=1,alpha=0(font_digits_letters)

<h2 class="ref-section" id="player-bat">Player bat</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The #R$E100(bat) in its normal, expanded and missile forms, and the
#R$E180(missile shot).
</div>

<div class="sprite-stage">
<div class="sprite-take">#UDGARRAY2,7,4,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E101,,2;$E100,,2;$E111,,2;$E110,,2)(player_bat)<div class="sprite-phase">normal bat</div></div>
<div class="sprite-take">#UDGARRAY2,7,4,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E121,,2;$E120,,2;$E131,,2;$E130,,2;$E141,,2;$E140,,2;$E151,,2;$E150,,2)(bat_expanded)<div class="sprite-phase">expanded bat</div></div>
<div class="sprite-take">#UDGARRAY2,7,4,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E161,,2;$E160,,2;$E171,,2;$E170,,2)(missile_bat)<div class="sprite-phase">missile bat</div></div>
<div class="sprite-take">#UDGARRAY2,7,4,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E181,,2;$E180,,2;$E191,,2;$E190,,2)(spr_missile_shot)<div class="sprite-phase">missile shot</div></div>
</div>

<h2 class="ref-section" id="ball">Ball</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The #R$E0E0(ball).
</div>

#UDGARRAY2,7,4,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E0E1,,2;$E0E0,,2;$E0F1,,2;$E0F0,,2)(ball)

<h2 class="ref-section" id="walls-playfield-frame">Walls / playfield frame</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The indestructible #R$95E0(border) around the brick interior. It is built from
tile glyphs. The colors below are the ones the game writes.
</div>

<h3 class="ref-subsection" id="side-wall">Side wall</h3>

<div class="paragraph">
The #R$969C(band) down the edge opposite the bat. It has the same pattern and
colors on either edge. Within the band the left column is bright cyan and the right
bright green. The band repeats every 8 rows. One period is rendered here:
</div>

#UDGARRAY2,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($D9A8;$D9B0,68;$D9D8;$D9E0,68;$D9A8;$D9B0,68;$D998;$D9A0,68;$D9B8;$D9C0,68;$D9B8;$D9C0,68;$D998;$D9A0,68;$D9D8;$D9E0,68)(side_wall)

<h3 class="ref-subsection" id="top-bottom-strip">Top / bottom strip</h3>

<div class="paragraph">
The #R$9667(strip) along the top and bottom edges. On both edges, its upper row is
bright cyan and its lower row bright green. It is five segments. Each opens on a post cell, closes on an end cell, and holds
plain cells between them. The second and fourth segments also hold two cells of
a second fill. Rendered here is the center segment, both rows:
</div>

#UDGARRAY8,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($D928;$D930;$D930;$D930;$D930;$D930;$D930;$D940;$D948,68;$D950,68;$D950,68;$D950,68;$D950,68;$D950,68;$D950,68;$D960,68)(border_strip)

<h3 class="ref-subsection" id="corners">Corners</h3>

<div class="paragraph">
The four #R$9610(corner blocks), all bright cyan. Rendered here as they sit on the
playfield:
</div>

#UDGTABLE
{ #UDGARRAY2,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($D908;$D910;$D918;$D920)(corner_tl) | #UDGARRAY2,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($D978;$D980;$D9E8;$D9F0)(corner_tr) }
{ #UDGARRAY2,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($D9F8;$DA00;$D988;$DA08)(corner_bl) | #UDGARRAY2,69,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($DA10;$DA18;$DA20;$D990)(corner_br) }
TABLE#

<h2 class="ref-section" id="bricks">Bricks</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The brick field is a 9×9 grid of bricks. A brick is a 2×2 block of tile glyphs plus
one color. Each design appears in up to seven inks, and the brick fixes its ink.
The table below shows each design once. The #R$921A(tile-glyph groups) entry
renders each one in every ink it takes.
</div>

#UDGTABLE(default)
{ =h Design | =h Brick | =h Slot codes | =h Class | =h Colors (inks used in levels) }
{ solid | #UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DDB0;$DDB8;$DDC0;$DE60)(brick_solid) | $04–$50 | 1, 7–15 | blue, red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow, white }
{ window | #UDGARRAY2,65,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DDC8;$DDD0;$DDD8;$DDE0)(brick_window) | $51–$57 | 1 | blue, red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow, white }
{ rounded | #UDGARRAY2,66,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DDE8;$DDF0;$DDF8;$DE00)(brick_rounded) | $58–$5E | 1 | red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow, white }
{ ornate | #UDGARRAY2,66,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DE08;$DE10;$DE18;$DE20)(brick_ornate) | $5F–$65 | 1 | red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow, white }
{ hatched | #UDGARRAY2,66,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD28;$DD30;$DD38;$DD40)(brick_hatch) | $6D–$73 | 1 | red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow, white }
{ <b>golden</b> | #UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAC8;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(brick_golden) | $01 | 2 <span class="dim">(top-left $59)</span> | cyan }
{ <b>silver-1</b> | #UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAF8;$DAD0;$DB00;$DB08)(brick_silver1) | $02 | 3 <span class="dim">(top-left $5F)</span> | cyan }
{ <b>silver-2</b> | #UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DB18;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(brick_silver2) | $03 | 5 <span class="dim">(top-left $63)</span> | cyan }
TABLE#

#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DA88;$DA88;$DA88;$DA88)(*sh0)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DA90;$DA90;$DA90;$DA90)(*sh1)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DA98;$DA98;$DA98;$DA98)(*sh2)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAA0;$DAA0;$DAA0;$DAA0)(*sh3)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAA8;$DAA8;$DAA8;$DAA8)(*sh4)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAB0;$DAB0;$DAB0;$DAB0)(*sh5)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAB8;$DAB8;$DAB8;$DAB8)(*sh6)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAC0;$DAC0;$DAC0;$DAC0)(*sh7)#UDGARRAY2,71,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($D900;$D900;$D900;$D900)(*sh8)

<div class="paragraph">
<div class="inset">#FRAMES(sh0,6;sh1,6;sh2,6;sh3,6;sh4,6;sh5,6;sh6,6;sh7,6;sh8,6)(brick_shatter)</div>
Shatter – the animation a brick plays as it is destroyed. It is the plain shatter
in the #R$AB60(break-animation table). The brick's design is gone from the first
sub-frame. All four quadrants take the same tile.
</div>

#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD48;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt0)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD50;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt1)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD58;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt2)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD60;$DD68;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt3)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD70;$DD78;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt4)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD60;$DD68;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt5)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD58;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt6)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD50;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt7)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD48;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt8)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DAC8;$DAD0;$DAD8;$DAE0)(*gt9)

<div class="paragraph">
<div class="inset">#FRAMES(gt0,6;gt1,6;gt2,6;gt3,6;gt4,6;gt5,6;gt6,6;gt7,6;gt8,6;gt9,6)(golden_twinkle)</div>
Golden-brick twinkle – the golden brick's #R$B0BF(idle flash).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The omitted angry-face brick and golden-brick gleam are shown under
#LINK(UnusedResources)(Unused resources).
</div>

<h3 class="ref-subsection" id="prizes">Prizes</h3>

#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DE48,$45;$DE50,$45;$DE58,$45;$DE60,$45)(*pz0)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DE68,$45;$DE70,$45;$DE78,$45;$DE80,$45)(*pz1)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DE88,$45;$DE90,$45;$DE98,$45;$DEA0,$45)(*pz2)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($D900,$45;$DEA8,$45;$D900,$45;$DEB0,$45)(*pz3)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DEB8,$46;$DEC0,$44;$DEC8,$46;$DED0,$44)(*pz4)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DED8,$46;$DEE0,$44;$DEE8,$46;$DEF0,$44)(*pz5)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DEF8,$46;$DF00,$44;$DF08,$46;$DF10,$44)(*pz6)

<div class="paragraph">
<div class="inset">#FRAMES(pz0,6;pz1,6;pz2,6;pz3,6;pz4,6;pz5,6;pz6,6)(prize_reveal)</div>
The reveal – the animation a prize brick plays as it gives up its prize. Every
prize plays it; only the glyph left in the cell at the end differs, as the
glyphs below show.
</div>


#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DCA8,$46;$DCB0,$44;$DCB8,$46;$DCC0,$44)(*sb0)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DCC8,$46;$DCD0,$44;$DCD8,$46;$DCE0,$44)(*sb1)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DCE8,$46;$DCF0,$44;$DCF8,$46;$DD00,$44)(*sb2)#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD08,$46;$DD10,$44;$DD18,$46;$DD20,$44)(*sb3)
